      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for packers and movers bangalore to pune</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The destination delivery handover for an automobile or car is a critical checkpoint that ensures the vehicle arrives in the same condition as it left the origin point.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This process combines a daylight condition re‑inspection, odometer verification against the load‑release (LR) bilty, and a signed condition sign‑off.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The steps below outline a thorough, repeatable handover procedure.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑Inspection</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Schedule the inspection during full daylight to eliminate shadows and glare that can obscure damage.</li>
      <li>Retrieve the original pickup photographs and the inspection checklist used at origin.</li>
      <li>Conduct a walk‑around of the vehicle, comparing each exterior surface, interior cabin, and glass panel with the corresponding pickup photo.</li>
      <li>Note any new scratches, dents, or interior wear; photograph any discrepancies with a timestamp.</li>
      <li>Confirm that all accessories (spare tire, jack, manuals) are present and undamaged.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Odometer Verification</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Locate the odometer reading on the vehicle’s instrument cluster.</li>
      <li>Reference the LR bilty, which records the mileage at the point of loading.</li>
      <li>Compare the current reading with the LR mileage; the difference should reflect the expected distance traveled plus a small tolerance (typically ±5 km) for rounding.</li>
      <li>If the reading exceeds the tolerance, investigate potential tampering, odometer roll‑back, or recording errors before proceeding.</li>
      <li>Record the verified mileage on the handover form and attach a photo of the odometer display.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑Off</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Present the completed inspection checklist, photographic evidence, and odometer verification to the receiving party.</li>
      <li>Both the carrier’s representative and the receiver must review each item and confirm agreement.</li>
      <li>Each party signs and dates the handover document, acknowledging that the vehicle’s condition matches the documented state.</li>
      <li>Provide a copy of the signed document to the shipper, the carrier, and retain one for internal records.</li>
      <li>Store all supporting photos and forms in the shipment’s digital file for future reference or dispute resolution.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<p>By following this structured handover—daylight re‑inspection, precise odometer verification, and a mutually signed condition sign‑off—stakeholders can confidently confirm that the vehicle has been delivered without undisclosed damage or mileage discrepancies, reducing claims and enhancing trust across the logistics chain.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



